          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Ascent</strong><br>\nSimone Veil began her political career by joining the French Ministry of Justice. She quickly moved up the ranks, becoming a prominent figure in French politics. Her intelligence and experience made her a respected voice in the government.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Health Minister of France</strong><br>\nIn 1974, Simone was appointed as the Health Minister of France, becoming the first woman to hold this position. During her tenure, she advocated for women's rights, including the right to access contraception and abortion, leading to the passage of the \"Veil Law\" in 1975.</p>\n\n<p><strong>European Parliament President</strong><br>\nSimone's political success continued as she was elected to the European Parliament. In 1979, she achieved another milestone by becoming the first elected President of the European Parliament, a role in which she served until 1982.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
