          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Remembering the Holocaust</strong><br>\nThroughout her life, Simone Veil remained a dedicated advocate for remembering the Holocaust and educating the public about its tragedies. She spoke openly about her experiences and worked towards Holocaust remembrance and education.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Return to French Politics</strong><br>\nAfter serving in the European Parliament, Simone returned to French politics. She held various positions, including Minister of State and member of the Constitutional Council, contributing her vast experience to the nation's governance.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nSimone Veil passed away on June 30, 2017. She left behind a legacy as a trailblazer for women's rights, a dedicated European, and a tireless advocate for the values she believed in. Her life's work continues to inspire people around the world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
